ACKNOWLEDGMENTS

GLD Viewer is a desktop viewer for glTF 2.0 / GLB models built on top of
several open-source projects. It would not exist without them.

3D rendering is provided by Three.js (https://threejs.org), MIT-licensed,
bridged into React via react-three-fiber and @react-three/drei
(https://github.com/pmndrs/react-three-fiber), both MIT-licensed.

glTF / GLB metadata parsing on the Rust side is provided by the `gltf` crate
(https://crates.io/crates/gltf), MIT/Apache-2.0 dual-licensed. Recursive
folder scanning uses the `walkdir` crate (https://crates.io/crates/walkdir),
MIT/Unlicense dual-licensed.

The desktop shell is built with Tauri 2 (https://tauri.app), MIT/Apache-2.0
dual-licensed. The native folder picker is provided by `tauri-plugin-dialog`,
MIT/Apache-2.0 dual-licensed.

UI icons come from Lucide (https://lucide.dev), ISC-licensed. Body type is
set in Inter (https://rsms.me/inter), OFL-licensed.

State is managed with zustand (https://github.com/pmndrs/zustand),
MIT-licensed. Build tooling is Vite (https://vitejs.dev), MIT-licensed.

Their license terms apply to those components and are reproduced in their
respective sources.
